/*
===============================================================================
TransactionFraud_GNN schema v1
Target: TigerGraph 4.2.x
===============================================================================

Purpose
-------
Predict fraud for one payment transaction with a combined temporal GNN (TGN)
and heterogeneous relational GNN (R-GCN). Payment_Transaction is the supervised
event vertex. Its typed relations preserve the initiating/funding account, card, merchant,
location, device and IP roles needed by R-GCN message passing. event_seq is the
canonical clock used by TGN and every cutoff-safe query.

This is a fresh-graph DDL. It deliberately contains no loading job and no fixed
population or transaction count. The expected load covers three years and about
150,000 individuals, but those are measured data properties, never schema
constants.

Temporal contract
-----------------
* event_seq is unique, deterministic, dense from 1 through the transaction
  count, strictly positive, and ordered by (event_ts_ms, transaction_id).
* DATETIME is retained for operator readability. event_ts_ms is authoritative
  because DATETIME does not preserve sub-second ordering.
* Every transaction-participation edge repeats event_seq and event_ts_ms.
* Slowly changing edges are visible to seed s only when
    valid_from_seq <= s.event_seq
    AND (valid_to_seq == 0 OR s.event_seq < valid_to_seq).
  Static ownership/PII facts known at the authorization request may therefore
  be visible on the seed event itself. Historical transaction context always
  uses neighbor.event_seq < seed.event_seq.
* fraud_label and label_* are supervision metadata. No model feature/message
  query may read them.

Privacy and feature contract
----------------------------
Email, phone, address, identity-document, device and IP primary IDs must be
salted/tokenized before loading. Raw PII is not stored. IDs are join keys, never
numeric features. Protected attributes such as name, gender and ethnicity are
intentionally absent. No corpus-wide count, fraud rate, risk score derived from
future labels, embedding, or model output is persisted on an entity vertex.
Shared PII topology is sufficient for v1; entity-resolution, match, and unify
vertices or edges are intentionally outside this schema and may be added later
as an optional, separately versioned module.

All non-key attributes on persistent entity vertices are immutable
first-observation snapshots: their values must have been known no later than
the vertex's first_seen_seq/first_seen_ts_ms and must never be overwritten with
later state. A mutable observation (for example a later device OS, IP network,
merchant classification, or country) belongs on the contemporaneous
Payment_Transaction or in a separately versioned fact, not in-place here. This
is what makes full node-table export safe for historical sampling.

Cardinality contract (validated by tfgnn_validate_graph)
---------------------------------------------------------
Each Payment_Transaction has exactly one initiating/funding Account and one
Merchant acceptance endpoint, and at most one Card, Merchant_Location, canonical
Device and canonical source IP_Address. The Merchant is the receiving side; its
settlement account is not modeled as a second Account in v1.
Optional endpoints may be absent. A Device or IP_Address may be shared by many
transactions; bounded temporal sampling prevents those hubs from expanding an
R-GCN batch without limit. At the graph high-water mark, each Merchant has
exactly one cutoff-visible operating Party; historical non-overlapping operator
tenures may coexist. Each Account has at least one cutoff-visible owning Party;
multiple owners are allowed for joint accounts.
This scope is merchant-payment authorizations. True account-to-account transfers
or a single record funded by multiple accounts require role-specific relations in
a later schema version rather than overloading Transaction_From_Account.
===============================================================================
*/

CREATE GRAPH TransactionFraud_GNN()

USE GRAPH TransactionFraud_GNN

CREATE SCHEMA_CHANGE JOB transaction_fraud_gnn_schema_v1
FOR GRAPH TransactionFraud_GNN {

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Persistent customer and payment entities
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /* party_type vocabulary: individual, company, merchant_entity; unknown is
     permitted only when the source has not classified the party. */
  ADD VERTEX Party(
      PRIMARY_ID party_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      customer_since_ts_ms UINT DEFAULT 0,
      party_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      home_country STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Account(
      PRIMARY_ID account_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      opened_ts_ms UINT DEFAULT 0,
      account_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      base_currency STRING DEFAULT "",
      country_code STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Card(
      PRIMARY_ID card_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      issued_ts_ms UINT DEFAULT 0,
      card_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      card_network STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      card_product STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      is_virtual BOOL DEFAULT "false"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Merchant(
      PRIMARY_ID merchant_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      onboarded_ts_ms UINT DEFAULT 0,
      merchant_category_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      merchant_country STRING DEFAULT "",
      merchant_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      is_online BOOL DEFAULT "false"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Merchant_Location(
      PRIMARY_ID location_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      country_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      region_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      postal_code_prefix STRING DEFAULT "",
      latitude DOUBLE DEFAULT 0,
      longitude DOUBLE DEFAULT 0,
      has_coordinates BOOL DEFAULT "false"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Infrastructure entities. They are nodes because reuse is graph signal.
     Mutable reputation/vendor scores belong on Payment_Transaction as an
     event-time snapshot, not here as a current-state value.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  ADD VERTEX Device(
      PRIMARY_ID device_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      device_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      os_family STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      browser_family STRING DEFAULT "unknown"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX IP_Address(
      PRIMARY_ID ip_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      country_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      asn INT DEFAULT -1,
      network_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Tokenized PII value nodes. Shared values create traversable topology.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  ADD VERTEX Email(
      PRIMARY_ID email_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      domain STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Phone(
      PRIMARY_ID phone_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      country_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      line_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown"
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Address(
      PRIMARY_ID address_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      country_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      region_code STRING DEFAULT "",
      postal_code_prefix STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  ADD VERTEX Identity_Document(
      PRIMARY_ID document_id STRING,
      first_seen_seq UINT,
      first_seen_ts_ms UINT,
      document_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      issuing_country STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Label-bearing event vertex.

     amount_present separates a genuine zero from an unloaded/default amount.
     Optional event-time risk scores use -1 as an explicit unavailable sentinel.
     Current authorization response/status is intentionally absent: the scoring
     moment is the authorization request, before that response exists.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  ADD VERTEX Payment_Transaction(
      PRIMARY_ID transaction_id STRING,

      event_time DATETIME,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT,

      amount DOUBLE DEFAULT 0,
      amount_present BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      currency STRING DEFAULT "",
      transaction_type STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      channel STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      entry_mode STRING DEFAULT "unknown",
      card_present BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      is_cross_border BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      is_recurring BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      merchant_category_code STRING DEFAULT "",

      has_event_location BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      event_latitude DOUBLE DEFAULT 0,
      event_longitude DOUBLE DEFAULT 0,

      device_risk_score DOUBLE DEFAULT -1,
      ip_risk_score DOUBLE DEFAULT -1,

      fraud_label INT DEFAULT -1,
      label_known BOOL DEFAULT "false",
      label_available_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      label_available_ts_ms UINT DEFAULT 0,
      label_source STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH PRIMARY_ID_AS_ATTRIBUTE="true", STATS="OUTDEGREE_BY_EDGETYPE";

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Slowly changing ownership and tokenized-PII relations.

     valid_to_seq == 0 means no known end. There is intentionally no
     DISCRIMINATOR: the v1 contract represents one consolidated association per
     endpoint pair. If discontinuous tenures become a real source-data concept,
     they require a schema migration and a discriminator rather than silent
     overwrites.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Owns_Account(
      FROM Party, TO Account,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Account_Owned_By_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Account_Has_Card(
      FROM Account, TO Card,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Card_Belongs_To_Account";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_Email(
      FROM Party, TO Email,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Email_Belongs_To_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_Phone(
      FROM Party, TO Phone,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Phone_Belongs_To_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_Address(
      FROM Party, TO Address,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Address_Belongs_To_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_Identity_Document(
      FROM Party, TO Identity_Document,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Identity_Document_Belongs_To_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_Device(
      FROM Party, TO Device,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Device_Associated_With_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Has_IP(
      FROM Party, TO IP_Address,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="IP_Associated_With_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Party_Operates_Merchant(
      FROM Party, TO Merchant,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Merchant_Operated_By_Party";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Merchant_Has_Location(
      FROM Merchant, TO Merchant_Location,
      valid_from_seq UINT,
      valid_to_seq UINT DEFAULT 0,
      confidence FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
      source_system STRING DEFAULT ""
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Location_Belongs_To_Merchant";

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Per-transaction participation relations. These are canonical R-GCN edge
     types and the export surface used to build cuGraph heterogeneous stores.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_From_Account(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO Account,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Account_Initiated_Transaction";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_Used_Card(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO Card,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Card_Used_By_Transaction";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_At_Merchant(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO Merchant,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Merchant_Received_Transaction";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_At_Location(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO Merchant_Location,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Location_Observed_In_Transaction";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_Used_Device(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO Device,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="Device_Used_By_Transaction";

  ADD DIRECTED EDGE Transaction_From_IP(
      FROM Payment_Transaction, TO IP_Address,
      event_ts_ms UINT,
      event_seq UINT
  ) WITH REVERSE_EDGE="IP_Observed_In_Transaction";
}

RUN SCHEMA_CHANGE JOB transaction_fraud_gnn_schema_v1

/*
Expected queryable catalog after the job:
  12 vertex types
  16 forward edge types
  16 explicit reverse edge types

No loading job is part of this repository contract. After the independently
managed load completes, create/install the queries under gsql/queries and run
tfgnn_validate_graph before exporting or training.
*/
